Verdict: PASS. I wrote it to session_plan/eval_task_1.md, and every Checked line passes.

The diff does what the task asked. There is now one function, choose_agent_model, that decides which model a named agent runs on, in this order:
• The file's `model:`. inherit means the main model, even when sub_agent_model is set.
• Family aliases (haiku, sonnet, opus, fable, any case). With provider anthropic, an alias uses the main model if it's the same family. Otherwise it uses the newest matching id from yoagent's own preset list, so no id is typed by hand.
• Other providers. An alias or a claude-… id is never sent. The agent falls back to sub_agent_model, else the main model, and its answer starts with a note naming both models.
• No `model:` in the file. It runs on sub_agent_model, else the main model, which is the old behaviour.

What I ran:
• The binary. I made a temp project with an agent file set to model: haiku. yoyo agents showed model: haiku → claude-haiku-5-5. With --provider deepseek it showed haiku (falls back to deepseek-v4-pro: haiku is a Claude alias and the provider is deepseek).
